Helios DXVK fork: event-query latency trace (HELIOS_DXVK_EVENT_TRACE=1)

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0022 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

A CPU-bound D3D11 game that limits its frames in flight with an event query
spins on GetData until the GPU has finished an earlier frame. In CS2 that
spin is a large share of the render thread (GetData, DxvkEvent::test, the
game's own timing loop), so the frame time includes the latency from End to
the event becoming visible, and that latency has several stages: the CS
thread recording the event signal, the submission thread submitting the
command list that holds it, and the GPU (with NVK over RM) executing up to
it.

With HELIOS_DXVK_EVENT_TRACE=1, every D3D11_QUERY_EVENT wait on the
immediate context is timed (QPC) at End, when the CS thread records the
signal, after the submission of that command list (0019's after-submit
callback) and at the first GetData that returns S_OK. Every two seconds the
process log gets one line with the number of waits, the mean end->ready
time and its maximum, the mean of each stage (end->cs, cs->submit,
submit->ready) over the waits that saw all stages, and GetData calls per
wait. Without the variable there are no clock reads.

